# Location details

## Summary

An opened location: its name over the tabs for its details, attributes, media, documents and, for a venue, its seating layout. On the details tab staff change the location's fields in the admin's language, archive it and change its switches; a region is saved only by an admin of locations.

## Requirements

- **TABS** — An opened location shows its name above the tabs Details, Attributes, Media, Documents and, for a venue, Seating layout, and opens on Details. Where the project's `hiddenTabs` option names them, Attributes and Documents are left out.
- **OTHERLANG** — Where the location has no name or no description in the admin's language, the field is empty and shows the text of another language as its hint.
- **ARCHIVESWITCH** — The details have an "Archived" switch, except for a location the backend marks as one that must stay active.
- **REGIONSAVE** — A region is saved only by staff with `locations:role#admin`; for anyone else its Save is disabled.
- **KEEPATTRS** — Saving the details keeps the location's other attributes: its hatching pattern, a venue's room plans and a stadium's or hall's attribute values.
- **UPDATEDONE** — A saved location shows "Location updated"; a failure shows "Location update failed". Typed coordinates that are not a pair or out of range show their message and save nothing.
- **UPDATELEAVE** — Leaving the details tab with unsaved changes asks before the changes are lost.

## Tests

- A staff member without `locations:role#admin` sees Save disabled on a region, and enabled on a venue.
- Saving a location's German name leaves its English name and slug unchanged.
- Saving the details of a stadium leaves its attribute values and hatching pattern as they were.
- A venue shows the Seating layout tab; a region does not.
- With `hiddenTabs` holding `documents`, no Documents tab is shown.
- A location without a German name shows its English name as the hint of the empty name field in German.

## View: LocationDetails

### Summary

An opened location, with its tabs, and the details tab's fields.

### Display

- The location's name above its tabs, Seating layout only for a venue, Attributes and Documents unless the project's `hiddenTabs` option hides them — [reads](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[TABS]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[CONFIG])
- A location is shown when the staff member may see it — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCSEE])
- The fields of the create page in the admin's language, another language's name and description as hints where this one has none — [reads](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:LocationType), [reads](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:LocationCategory), [reads](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Country), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[OTHERLANG]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCNAME]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[WEB])
- The "Archived" switch, unless the location must stay active — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[ARCHIVESWITCH])
- Save is disabled on a region for staff without `locations:role#admin` — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[REGIONSAVE])
- Asks before unsaved changes are left — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[UPDATELEAVE])

### Actions

- Save — [exposes](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Operation:UpdateLocation)
- Attributes — [navigates](aim:juicebar.locations.attributes#View:AttributesTab)
- Media — [navigates](aim:juicebar.locations.media#View:LocationMedia)
- Documents — [navigates](aim:juicebar.locations.media#View:LocationDocuments)
- Seating layout — [navigates](aim:juicebar.locations.seating#View:SeatingLayout)

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/location-details.component.ts#LocationDetailsComponent` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/details-location/details-location.component.ts#DetailsLocationComponent` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/location-fields/location-fields.component.ts#LocationFieldsComponent` — as: component
- binds: `service:locations:service#getLocation` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: UpdateLocation

### Summary

A staff member changes a location's fields and switches in the admin's language.

### Input

```schema
locationId: string required ref(juicebar.locations#Location.id)
type: string required ref(juicebar.locations#LocationType.value)
location_category: string ref(juicebar.locations#LocationCategory.value)
name: string required
short_name: string
description: string
street: string
postcode: string
city: string
country: string ref(juicebar.locations#Country.id)
url: string
archived: boolean
organisation_visibility: boolean
accessibility: boolean
email: string
latitude: number
longitude: number
language: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationEditor`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationAdmin`
- `juicebar.locations#Persona:LocationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The name and the description in the given language are replaced, and the slug in that language is made again from the name — [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCNAME]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCSLUG]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[LANG])
- The type, the category, the short name, the address or the URL, the archived switch and the organisation-wide visibility are replaced — [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[WEB])
- The coordinates are the ones typed in where the project has the field, or else the address lookup's first match; when neither gives any, the stored ones stay — [invokes](aim:juicebar.locations#Capability:Geocoding), [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[COORDS])
- The location's other attributes stay; where the project's `fields` option names them, the email is set or, when emptied, removed, and the accessibility switch is replaced — [mutates](aim:juicebar.locations#Record:Location), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[KEEPATTRS]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[EXTRAS]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[CONFIG])
- A region reaches it only from staff with `locations:role#admin`; the backend makes no such check — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[REGIONSAVE])
- A notice tells whether it worked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations.details#Requirements[UPDATEDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `updated` permission, or for a location of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.locations#Requirements[LOCORG])

### Returns

- The stored location.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/details/details-location/details-location.component.ts#DetailsLocationComponent.save` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/location-form.ts#toLocationUpdate` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/locations/location-form.ts#resolveCoordinates` — as: component
- binds: `service:locations:service#updateLocation` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
